%U A401012 4,1,2,3,0,6,5,5,2,6,5,8,2,4,8,0,1,3,3,7,7,0,1,6,9,5,4,8,2,6,1,6,8,4,6,1,9
%N A401012 Decimal expansion of 1 - Sum_{n>=1} 2^(-floor(n*log_2(3))).
%C A401012 The digits of the binary expansion of 1 - c that equal 1 are exactly those with index floor(n*log_2(3)) = A056576(n), n >= 1. Because log_2(3) is irrational, these digits form a Sturmian word, which is what makes c transcendental (Ferenczi and Mauduit).
%C A401012 This is the case b = 2, alpha = log_2(3) of the sum Sum_{n>=1} b^(-floor(n*alpha)) introduced by Boehmer (1927). For every irrational alpha, Adams and Davison (1977) give the continued fraction of (b-1)*Sum_{n>=1} b^(-floor(n*alpha)) explicitly, which accounts for the unusually large partial quotients 0, 3, 2, 36, 2056, 70368878395648, ...
%H A401012 Joel Cruz Cabrera, <a href="/A401012/b401012.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..999</a>
%H A401012 W. W. Adams and J. L. Davison, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1090/S0002-9939-1977-0441879-4">A remarkable class of continued fractions</a>, Proc. Amer. Math. Soc. 65 (1977), 194-198.
%H A401012 P. E. Boehmer, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01209172">Ueber die Transzendenz gewisser dyadischer Brueche</a>, Math. Ann. 96 (1927), 367-377.
%H A401012 Joel Cruz Cabrera, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21516620">Three Exact Results Arising from Collatz-Type Dynamics: Valuation Equidistribution, Fermat Bases, and a Transcendental Density Constant</a>, Zenodo, 2026.
%H A401012 S. Ferenczi and C. Mauduit, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1006/jnth.1997.2175">Transcendence of numbers with a low complexity expansion</a>, J. Number Theory 67 (1997), 146-161.
%F A401012 Equals 1 - Sum_{n>=1} 2^(-A056576(n)).
%F A401012 Equals 1/2 - Sum_{n>=2} 2^(-floor(n*log_2(3))).
%e A401012 0.28627450232410874196766280129977342970092878554364...
%o A401012 (Python)
%o A401012 def A(nd=105):
%o A401012     K = 4*nd + 64
%o A401012     S, n = 0, 1
%o A401012     while (k := (3**n).bit_length() - 1) <= K:
%o A401012         S += 1 << (K - k); n += 1
%o A401012     return list(map(int, str((((1 << K) - S) * 10**nd) >> K).zfill(nd)))
%Y A401012 Cf. A020857, A056576, A402278.
%K A401012 nonn,cons,new
%O A401012 0,1
